IMPORT prelude

-- Public Trustee Act 1915 (Singapore) -- the administration of small estates (s 6(1)-(3), (6)-(8)), with the amount
-- prescribed for s 6(1) by rule 7A of the Public Trustee Rules and the procedure in rule 9.
--
-- Edition: Act -- 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PTA1915.txt.
-- Rules -- Public Trustee Rules (Cap. 260, R 1), informal consolidation, version in force from 1 April 2022, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/PTA1915-R1.txt. Rule 7A was inserted by S 864/2014 wef 31 December 2014. The figure "$5,000"
-- in rule 7A was read in the .txt deposit (pypdf) and again in a fresh pdftotext extraction of PTA1915-R1.pdf; both say
-- "$5,000". The heading of rule 9 ("Estate less than $5,000") and rule 9(1) repeat the same figure.
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0279 (Haziq scenario, event from the Haziq or Simone scenarios (supplied-fact entry)):
-- "A man dies intestate leaving $38,000 in a bank account and no property. May the Public Trustee administer the estate without
-- a grant, and up to what value?" The ledger expected $50,000. The deposited rule says $5,000, so on the Act and these Rules an
-- estate of $38,000 is OUTSIDE s 6(1).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 6(4) (administrative powers conferred by rules), s 6(5) (rule-making), s 6(9) (bank interest on small sums);
-- rule 8 (evidence the Public Trustee may require) except as the inputs below; rule 10 (opinion of the court); the amount
-- prescribed before 31 December 2014; any route to administration without a grant under other written law (for example the
-- Probate and Administration Act or the Intestate Succession Act, neither of which was read for this module); who takes the
-- estate on intestacy. The earlier module pta-trusts.l4 keeps its own s 6(1) rule with the amount as a parameter.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.
-- See NOTES.md.

§ `Public Trustee Act 1915 -- small estates`

§§ `Rules r 7A -- the prescribed amount`

-- r 7A: "For the purposes of section 6(1) of the Act, the prescribed amount is $5,000."
`the amount prescribed for section 6(1)` MEANS 5000

§§ `6(1) -- who may apply, and when the Public Trustee must administer`

-- s 6(1): "Any person who in the opinion of the Public Trustee would be entitled to apply to the court for an order for the
-- administration of an estate, the gross capital value of which is proved to the satisfaction of the Public Trustee to be less
-- than the prescribed amount, may apply to the Public Trustee to administer the estate, and where any such application is made,
-- and it appears to the Public Trustee that the persons beneficially entitled are persons of small means, the Public Trustee
-- must administer the estate, unless the Public Trustee sees good reason for refusing to do so."
-- "Less than" is strict: an estate of exactly $5,000 is outside.
GIVEN `gross capital value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the estate is within the small-estate amount` IF
    `gross capital value` < `the amount prescribed for section 6(1)`

GIVEN `applicant could apply to court for an administration order` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `gross capital value` IS A NUMBER,
      `value proved to the Public Trustee's satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 6(1) application may be made` IF
        `applicant could apply to court for an administration order`
    AND `value proved to the Public Trustee's satisfaction`
    AND `the estate is within the small-estate amount` `gross capital value`

GIVEN `applicant could apply to court for an administration order` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `gross capital value` IS A NUMBER,
      `value proved to the Public Trustee's satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `beneficiaries appear to be of small means` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Public Trustee sees good reason to refuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Public Trustee must administer under section 6(1)` IF
        `a section 6(1) application may be made` `applicant could apply to court for an administration order` `gross capital value` `value proved to the Public Trustee's satisfaction`
    AND `beneficiaries appear to be of small means`
    AND (NOT `Public Trustee sees good reason to refuse`)

§§ `Rules r 9(1) -- refusal`

-- r 9(1): "If it is not proved to the satisfaction of the Public Trustee that the gross capital value of the estate is less than
-- $5,000, or if it does not appear to him that the persons beneficially entitled are persons of small means, or if he sees any
-- other good reason for refusing the application, he shall refuse the application, and shall forthwith give notice to the
-- applicant of such refusal."
GIVEN `gross capital value` IS A NUMBER,
      `value proved to the Public Trustee's satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `beneficiaries appear to be of small means` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Public Trustee sees good reason to refuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Public Trustee must refuse the section 6 application` IF
        (NOT `value proved to the Public Trustee's satisfaction`)
    OR  (NOT `the estate is within the small-estate amount` `gross capital value`)
    OR  (NOT `beneficiaries appear to be of small means`)
    OR  `Public Trustee sees good reason to refuse`

-- r 9(3): "A refusal under this rule shall not prevent the Public Trustee from exercising with respect to the estate any powers
-- (other than the powers under section 6 of the Act) exerciseable by him ... if duly appointed to exercise those powers."
GIVEN `duly appointed to exercise other powers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `after a refusal the Public Trustee may still act under other powers` IF
    `duly appointed to exercise other powers`

§§ `6(2), (3) -- vesting and discharge`

-- s 6(2): "On the Public Trustee undertaking, by written declaration signed and sealed by him or her, to administer the estate,
-- the trust property vests, by virtue of this Act, in the Public Trustee."
-- s 6(8): where the court orders administration under s 6(6), "this section applies as if the Public Trustee has given an
-- undertaking under subsection (2)".
-- That the vesting is "by virtue of this Act", and so needs no grant of probate or letters, is an INFERENCE from these words;
-- the Act does not use the phrase "without a grant".
GIVEN `written declaration signed and sealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `court ordered administration under section 6(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trust property vests in the Public Trustee` IF
    `written declaration signed and sealed` OR `court ordered administration under section 6(6)`

-- s 6(3): "As from such vesting, any trustee entitled under the trust to administer the estate is discharged from all liability
-- attaching to the administration, except in respect of past acts."
GIVEN `property has vested in the Public Trustee` IS A BOOLEAN, `liability concerns a past act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the former trustee is discharged from the liability` IF
    `property has vested in the Public Trustee` AND (NOT `liability concerns a past act`)

§§ `6(6), (7) -- administration by order of the court, with no value limit`

-- s 6(6): "Where proceedings have been instituted in any court for the administration of an estate, the court may order the
-- Public Trustee to administer the estate ... where it appears to the court that -- (a) by reason of the small value of the
-- estate, the estate can be more economically administered by the Public Trustee than by any other person; or (b) for any other
-- reason, it is expedient that the estate should be administered by the Public Trustee instead of any other person."
-- s 6(7): "The court must, before making any order under subsection (6), consider the views of the Public Trustee on the matter."
-- No amount is prescribed for s 6(6).
GIVEN `administration proceedings instituted` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `more economical by reason of small value` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `expedient for any other reason` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `court considered the Public Trustee's views` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order the Public Trustee to administer` IF
        `administration proceedings instituted`
    AND (`more economical by reason of small value` OR `expedient for any other reason`)
    AND `court considered the Public Trustee's views`

§§ `REQ-0279 -- which part of section 6 an estate can use`

GIVEN `gross capital value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
`the section 6 route for an estate of` `gross capital value` MEANS
    IF `the estate is within the small-estate amount` `gross capital value`
    THEN "s 6(1): application to the Public Trustee, who must administer if the beneficiaries are of small means and there is no good reason to refuse"
    ELSE "not s 6(1): only by court order under s 6(6), on proceedings already instituted"
